{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Doubled.</b> Mori HaRav Yosef, of blessed memory, says that both of them were one upon the other, and in the upper one the stones were set, and the lower one was bonded to it to strengthen, so that the stones set in the hollowed settings within the upper one would not be spoiled. And so it is taught in Torat Kohanim in the parashah of וכי תקריב קרבן מנחה: ועשית חשן משפט וגו׳ — one might think that just as this [ephod] is doubled, so too that [choshen] is doubled; therefore it says זהב — זהב it requires [i.e., it must be of gold] but not to double it. That is, the ephod was not to be doubled like the choshen. And Rashi too explained, regarding ונתת אל חשן המשפט את האורים ואת התומים: Urim — from the language of kingdoms/regions, as in באורים כבדו השם. Tumim — the language of boundaries, for there the boundary of each and every tribe would be completed within the choshen — the territory and boundary and borders of each and every tribe within its stone. And thus it says משפט בני ישראל, so that they could not contest one another at all. And in the days of Joshua, when they cast lots, the lot fell as written in the choshen. And also the priest would discern through ruach ha-kodesh, and in time of war and in time of need the letters would rise up and speak and answer them every question they asked."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:14.030262720Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}